\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The rules steer the chemistry. Left: the compiled objective weights---a deterministic rule-compilation (a heuristic keyed by the agent's derived category, effectively three buckets, not continuously tuned). The ``rigidity'' term rewards \emph  {fewer} rotatable bonds; the real separator is the per-class rotatable-bond setpoint (rot$\leq $5/10/14), shown by each class. ISAC's stability weight is floored to paramount by the low-evidence safety gate. Right: the generated designs separate by class, driven mainly by the rigidity setpoint (x); y is the per-molecule Ertl SA subscore (a real quantity, not jitter).\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:steer}{{3}{5}{The rules steer the chemistry. Left: the compiled objective weights---a deterministic rule-compilation (a heuristic keyed by the agent's derived category, effectively three buckets, not continuously tuned). The ``rigidity'' term rewards \emph {fewer} rotatable bonds; the real separator is the per-class rotatable-bond setpoint (rot$\leq $5/10/14), shown by each class. ISAC's stability weight is floored to paramount by the low-evidence safety gate. Right: the generated designs separate by class, driven mainly by the rigidity setpoint (x); y is the per-molecule Ertl SA subscore (a real quantity, not jitter).\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Stress-test of the confidence metric: varying retrieval depth (top-$k$) leaves each class's confidence stable---the ARC rule stays contested ($\approx $0.33) at every $k$. Reproducible, not a lucky $k$.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sens}{{4}{5}{Stress-test of the confidence metric: varying retrieval depth (top-$k$) leaves each class's confidence stable---the ARC rule stays contested ($\approx $0.33) at every $k$. Reproducible, not a lucky $k$.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Cathepsin-B co-fold (affinity indexes recognition, not cleavage). The cleavable Val-Cit designs (cytotoxin, and the held-out-derived ARC linker) are recognised in the clinical-substrate regime; the rigid ARC design binds $>$10$\times $ weaker---the in-silico feasibility proof.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cofold}{{5}{5}{Cathepsin-B co-fold (affinity indexes recognition, not cleavage). The cleavable Val-Cit designs (cytotoxin, and the held-out-derived ARC linker) are recognised in the clinical-substrate regime; the rigid ARC design binds $>$10$\times $ weaker---the in-silico feasibility proof.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
